<!--Post: 11290--><!--Time: 1110557971-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11290"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 8:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the media want to discuss his reputation as a good guy for the sake of analyzing how he evaded capture or why he was BTK, I understand that. But if I have to read one more interview in which someone sobbingly asserts, &#34;Rader saved my life! [or &#34;my puppy!&#34;]&#34;, I&#39;m going to vomit all over my computer. I&#39;d like to start this thread so anyone who wants can post information on all the sneaky, nasty little things he did to his neighbors, and we can even out the testimonials.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/11062626.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/11062626.htm</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11290-->
<!--Post: 11329--><!--Time: 1110590476-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11329"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 5:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My favorite was when he went to the house of the ill person and measured their lawn with a ruler. THEN wrote them a citation for it<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11329-->
<!--Post: 11346--><!--Time: 1110599435-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11346"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 7:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The time he had given a woman a citation for something.  The night before court, he walked right into her house.... WITHOUT KNOCKING....says &#34;Don&#39;t forget you have court in the morning...&#34; then turns around and leaves. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11346-->
<!--Post: 11348--><!--Time: 1110600594-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11348"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 8:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Be patient Frey, <BR> <BR>When the family begins to talk... and they will... <BR>We are going to hear some wicked, wicked s&#42;%t! <BR> <BR>LaterDog <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11348-->
<!--Post: 11353--><!--Time: 1110606439-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11353"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 9:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->...let&#39;s not forget the multiple people who LEFT TOWN because of his antics.  Even psychotic stalker ex-boyfriends and witness-murdering criminals rarely score higher than a &#34;1&#34; in terroristic evictions.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11353-->
<!--Post: 11354--><!--Time: 1110607096-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11354"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 9:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some thoughts on the story that you posted the link to Freya, <BR> He wouldn&#39;t have had to place himself and the boy in the position of almost drowning as he fought the current for 10 minutes before bringing the canoe to shore if he hadn&#39;t overloaded the canoe with all his anal retentive junk in the first place. Le Voyager BTK. <BR> <BR>&#34;He was the nicest guy in the world.&#34;...Gary Dusen. <BR>Well guess what Gary? He wasn&#39;t. <BR> <BR>&#34;He would keep a confidence.&#34;...Margaret McDowel. <BR>Yeah Margaret, and a secret too, and a necklace, and a drivers license. <BR> <BR>&#34;I hope your mommy will be OK.&#34;...Dennis Rader to Deane Harris. <BR>He&#39;d hate to see her expire to diabetes when he&#39;s been possibly considering her as a future potential BTK victim. <BR>And what&#39;s up with him showing a distressed 11 year old where his phone was so she could call 911 for her mother? Couldn&#39;t he have done that himself while his wife comforted and calmed down the girl. <BR> <BR>The biggest hero of the story is Shadow the dog who lived to an old age and despised Dennis Rader his entire life.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11354-->
<!--Post: 11356--><!--Time: 1110607512-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 10:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->10-4 on Shadow.  Like Lassie, &#40;s&#41;he spotted the danger, but the humans were too stupid to understand.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11356-->
<!--Post: 11365--><!--Time: 1110609339-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11365"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 10:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The a&#42;&#42;h&#42;&#42;&#42; could have been Pope Dennis I, and lived his entire life like Mother Theresa and die like Ghunga Din, but if there is a Hell, and if I was the entity that makes the decision &#40;I am not familiar with the proceedings of the Court of Heaven and Hell&#41;, I would sentence him to eternity in Hell, just for the 2 hours and 15 minutes he spent at the Otero&#39;s. <BR> <BR>If it should turn out that he actually does have multiple personalities, the Monster would get eternity in Hell and I&#39;d still give the good Dennis 100,000 years for aiding and abetting.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11365-->
<!--Post: 11384--><!--Time: 1110647532-->
